commit 0364b7687a355af2c28b964e4a33a24907264c02
Author: jingjiangze <1689170897@qq.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 10 11:55:55 2026 +0800

    perf(net): the m.public hot frame drops the per-match constants (baseline + merge)
    
    A client that merges. The broadcast m.public is 98% of the bytes a seat receives in the
    default clientCombat path, and every frame is deflated independently
    (serverNoContextTakeover), so anything constant inside a frame costs its compressed size
    in EVERY frame. Ten fields are fixed at match start and never change afterwards
    (lastRound, modeId, difficulty, stageId, factions, disabledBonds, drawnDisabledBonds,
    bannedChess, bossId, hiddenBossId) - measured over five matches across co-op
    NORMAL/HARD/ABYSS, solo and the 协同共竞 variant.
    
    The hot frame is now compact (views.js publicView({full:false})): 4,799 B vs 5,653 B,
    15.1% off every frame. The constants travel in a BASELINE (full:true) that the client
    resets its mirror from - sent by start() to every human seat before the first compact
    frame, and by _resync on every join / reconnect / spectator-add. The client merges instead
    of replacing (main.js), so a compact frame can no longer erase what the baseline gave it.
    
    Fallbacks, in the shape the snapshot rate already uses (server/match/snapRate.js):
      * the capability is DECLARED per socket - hello.pub (shared/protocol.js), re-declared on
        every hello so a resume with an older/newer client is re-evaluated;
      * a session that does not declare it gets the full frame instead, every time
        (Lobby.broadcastRoom), so an old client, a third-party client or a page still running
        the pre-deploy JS sees exactly what it sees today;
      * the replay a resume gets keeps the full frame too (ctx.lastPublicFull), or the result
        screen would be replayed a frame without difficulty/bannedChess.
    
    hello.version stays strictly checked: the capability is a new OPTIONAL field, never a
    version bump.
    
    Verified: test/match/connection + lobby-integration 18/18 (the constants test now asserts
    the baseline carries them and the hot frame drops them).

